<title>LITHUANIA: COMMISSION REGISTERS GAS FIRM CAPITAL BOOST.</title>
<headline>COMMISSION REGISTERS GAS FIRM CAPITAL BOOST.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Lithuanian securities commission said on Friday that its extraordinary meeting had registered a 4.96 million litas share capital issue for Lithuanian Gas.</p>
<p>&quot;The current share capital of the firm is 333.78 million litas and it will stand at 338.74 million litas,&quot; Dalius Shimenas, the spokesman for the commission, told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;The issue will be made from additional contributions,&quot; Shimenas added.</p>
<p>State-run Lithuanian Gas, the country's major distributor of natural gas, is one of the major shares on the Vilnius bourse.</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 22 35 17</p>
